{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "description": "Aerial GPU Benchmark CICD case database. This is the source of truth for SM allocation, expected cell capacity, and run settings for the 80000-series configs. Each case carries an 'enabled' flag: run_cicd_cases.py --case all runs only enabled cases unless --include-disabled is passed, while an explicitly selected case id always runs. Per-GPU values live under each case's gpu_configs map; the runner picks the entry matching the detected GPU. The default operating points are GH200 at 1000 MHz and RTX_PRO_4500 at 1610 MHz; the freq/power/target defaults embedded in the case YAMLs are the RTX_PRO_4500 values for direct measure.py runs. A gpu_configs entry MAY contain an optional 'alt_freqs' map of developer-tuned operating points at non-default frequencies (keyed by MHz, e.g. 1980 for GH200); these are reference-only and are intentionally NOT run by CICD -- run_cicd_cases.py reads only the top-level entry, while run_sm_opt.py produces/consumes alt_freqs. To make an alternate frequency the CICD default, promote its values to the top-level entry. Case numbering: the last digit selects the base case and the tens digit selects the variant family (8000x = base, 8001x = base + early HARQ, 8002x = base + cuMAC in a green context). The cuMAC green-context cases carry a 6th SM entry for MAC; their SM allocations are manually tuned and run_sm_opt.py does not apply to them. A green-context gpu_configs entry additionally carries green_context_sm_alloc, a per-channel map of [split_start, sm_count] green-context split parameters. The testbench reads these ranges only from its YAML (not CLI args), so the generated wrapper script materializes a temp YAML in the run dir with the detected GPU's ranges appended at the root (root-level overrides any config-level block in the case YAML) and runs measure.py against it. Unlike MPS sm_allocation counts, green-context ranges partition the GPU exclusively unless splits deliberately overlap; keep sm_allocation consistent with the [start, count] ranges.",
  "defaults": {
    "usecase": "F08",
    "function_slots": 20,
    "function_cells": 2,
    "confirm_slots": 300,
    "power_start": 1,
